  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed dwelling, by reason of its proximity to the western boundary of the site, scale and crown roof form, would appear as a cramped and visually intrusive form of development that would be at odds with the established pattern of housing at corner plots in the locality, resulting in the loss of the existing open and spacious character at the junction between Leigh Drive and Aylsham Lane. The proposed development would therefore be contrary to Local Plan Policy 26 as well as Policy DP3(1) of the NPPF.",
    "In the event that this application is allowed through the appeals process, the proposals would be liable for the following CIL contributions:",
    "Mayoral CIL (MCIL2) contribution of £1,925 (x £25 per sqm).",
    "Havering CIL (HCIL) contribution of £9,625 (x £125 per sqm)",
    "Each contribution would be subject to indexation.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, notification of intended refusal and the reason for it was given to the agent via email on 19/10/2026.",
    "The Local Planning Authority has acted positively and proactively in determining this application by assessing the proposal against all material planning considerations, including planning policies and any representations which were received.  It subsequently determined to grant planning permission in accordance with the National Planning Policy requirement that applications for sustainable development are approved where possible.  A detailed analysis of the scheme is set out in the report on the application prepared by officers."
  ]
